    </description>
    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">RPD Output Indicator 2.1.4
Number of parliamentary &amp; judicial institutions supported to promote inclusion, effectiveness, transparency, and accountability

Project Output indicators
1. Number of country-to-country partnerships and knowledge transfers facilitated: 1 (2021)
2. Number of courts conducting self-assessments using tools produced or promoted by JIN-ASEAN: 2 (2019)
3. Number of policy level changes or administrative/ process level changes informed by the findings and recommendations of the research studies on gendered threats: 0 (2021)</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">RPD Output Indicator 2.1.4
Number of parliamentary &amp; judicial institutions supported to promote inclusion, effectiveness, transparency, and accountability: 5 by 2025</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2022 JIN ASEAN works with Supreme Courts and Courts of Justice in Indonesia, Lao PDR, Thailand, and Vietnam to enhance judicial integrity and promote court excellence, particularly focusing on transparency, integrity, and accountability.

More info, if needed:
In Vietnam, activities include: Workshops training judges on the IFCE Self-Assessment process. Completion of the Self-Assessment. Pilot of a project in response to the IFCE Action Plan. Training and tools for judicial excellence implications of new technologies
In Indonesia, activities include: Revision of the whistle-blower dashboard for reporting and tracking responses to corruption to include greater responsiveness, training for the judiciary and staff involved. Education about and whistleblowing on sextortion and gendered experiences of corruption will be added to the anti-corruption approach.
In Thailand, activities include: Capacity-building for the judicial sector on digital transformation and gender equality to improve integrity and inclusive justice in Thailand. Developing a pilot court to implement recommendations from the self-assessment of the International Framework for Court Excellence.
In Lao PDR, activities include: IFCE Self-Assessment and action planning, linked to judicial capacity building and designed to inform opportunities from donors and partners to develop the case management systems nationally.

Project Output indicators
1. Number of country-to-country partnerships and knowledge transfers facilitated: 1 (2021); 2 (2022)
In 2022, the project organised a workshop for over 150 judges in Thailand &#x201c;Promoting Judicial Integrity Through Digital Transformation&#x201d; and a regional Knowledge Exchange Session on the IFCE Self-Assessment with National Center for State Courts.

2. Number of courts conducting self-assessments using tools produced or promoted by JIN-ASEAN: 2 (2019) 3 (2022)
In 2022 JIN ASEAN is supporting judiciaries in Lao PDR, Thailand and Vietnam in conducting IFCE self-assessment exercises. 

3. Number of policy level changes or administrative/ process level changes informed by the findings and recommendations of the research studies on gendered threats: 0 (2021) 0 (2022)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
